X-SOURCE:Meetup: NJ Bowling, Volleyball, Tennis & More
UID:event_315934589@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260822T020943Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260829T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260829T180000
SUMMARY:Casual Volleyball - North Jersey
DESCRIPTION:North Jersey Bowling\, Volleyball\, Tennis & More\nWe're a gro
 up of people who will start by hitting the ball around for the first 20-30
  minutes and then will break up into 2-4 teams for two or three hours of p
 lay.\n\nIf we have more than 20 people show up\, we'll break up into three
  or four teams of 6 (Some may have 7\, 8 or 9. Additional players just rot
 ate into play). Games will be to 15 points. Rally scoring. Winner stays on
  (unless a team has won four straight).\n\nWe'll be heading outdoors to th
 e hard court in Leonia off Overpeck County Pk Driveway in the Overpeck Cou
 nty Park.\n\n\\*\\*\\*After playing\, we'll be likely heading to Tropical 
 Juice Bar\, an idea of regular attendee Kate\, for a drink and snack. It's
  located at 60 River St. in Hackensack. Feel free to join us or suggest an
 other spot for a post-volleyball hangout. \\*\\*\\*\n\nThere's no fee to p
 lay volleyball and nothing else you need to do besides show up. Come anyti
 me!! All are welcome!!!\n\nThis is a casual play. We're not in a league an
 d are not here to analyze your form. Most of us are average at best\, and 
 some haven't played in months\, maybe years\, and just want to occasionall
 y play again and hang out.\n\nDirections: You can Google "Volleyball Court
  in Leonia" and it should come up. Or type 41 Willow Tree Road\, Leonia\, 
 NJ 07605 into your GPS\, but note that it's not on Willow Tree Road\, just
  near it. Instead\, turn onto Overpeck County Pk Driveway off Fort Lee Roa
 d (Degraw Avenue). It is past the tennis courts and near a basketball cour
 t and track. You can try Googling "Leonia High School" as well. That shoul
 d help you find it. You can go to the back high school parking lot and the
 n cross over the train tracks.\n\nPlease note. We don't have the court res
 erved and if it happens to be taken\, we may play with those already occup
 ying it or we will try to relocate on the fly. It's certainly possible tha
 t we may have to cancel that day if we can't find a suitable spot. And if 
 it's looking like it'll rain or snow\, I'll make a call on whether to canc
 el around an hour ahead of the scheduled start time.\n\nPlease bring a bal
 l and net if you have them for possible use during the game. Feel free to 
 bring a speaker for music\, or snacks and drinks for consumption during pl
 ay.\n\nIf you have trouble finding the court or group\, you can call or te
 xt Andy Milone at 201-234-9609. There is plenty of parking and an open bat
 hroom at the park.\n\nHope you'll join us for our 21st casual volleyball e
 vent. Questions or comments? You can message Andy on Meetup\, or call/text
  him at 201-234-9609. Check out bowling\, soccer\, volleyball\, tennis or 
 one of our other activities at: www.meetup.com/north-jersey-bowling-soccer
 -volleyball\n\nIf interested in staying touch with group members or conver
 sing about future events\, feel free to inquire about our WhatsApp group c
 hat.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/north-jersey-bowling-soccer-volleybal
 l/events/315934589/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
